  "title": "Hot Cross Buns - Alternating Bass",
  "bpm": 50,
  "beatsPerMeasure": 4,
  "showChordNames": false,
  "lesson": {
    "instructions": "Use your thumb (p) to alternate two bass notes: open low E, then B on the A string at fret 2. Use your index or middle finger for the familiar melody on the thin high E string, frets 4, 2 and 0. Prepare A-string fret 2 before its bass note, then move to the melody positions as needed.\n\nAfter the count-in, bars 3-4 practise the first melody note together with E bass, then B bass: hold each pair for two beats and rest for two. Bars 5-12 play the whole tune twice. Add bass on the first beat of bars 5, 6, 8, 9, 10 and 12: E, B, E, B, E, B. Keep the quicker middle bars melody only.\n\nVertically aligned TAB numbers mean play together. Follow the written bass and keep alternating across repeats. Each note has its own colour and result. Start slowly at 50 BPM; a quiet or unclear note may stay yellow.",
